# Searching and resizing with a multi-line prompt: the search prompt
# replaces only the last line of the prompt.
tags: search display prompt
--- script
add_history "first entry"
add_history "second entry"
readline "top line\nbottom> "

=== isearch-multiline-prompt
tags: reverse-search-history
keys: \C-rfir<snap>\C-g<snap>\r

=== isearch-multiline-prompt-accept
tags: reverse-search-history
keys: \C-rsec<snap>\e<pause>X<snap>\r

=== noninc-search-multiline-prompt
tags: non-incremental-reverse-search-history
keys: \M-pfirst<snap>\r<snap>\r

=== forward-isearch-multiline-prompt
tags: forward-search-history
keys: <up><up>\C-ssec<snap>\r

=== resize-multiline-prompt
tags: SIGWINCH display
keys: abc<resize:40x10><snap>d<snap>\r

=== resize-multiline-prompt-wrapped
tags: SIGWINCH display
screen: 30x10
keys: 0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz<resize:20x10><snap>\C-a<snap>\r

=== resize-multiline-prompt-invisible
tags: SIGWINCH display
--- script
readline "\001\e[1m\002title\001\e[0m\002\nbottom> "
--- keys
abc<resize:50x10><snap>\r
